eated [`D0003`](../authoring-runbooks/D0003.md) as its sole\n+successor, without advancing B/R counters or modifying accepted work.\n+\n ## Dispatcher checkpoint \u2014 D0001\n \n D0001 expanded no chapter and allocated no B/R contracts. `SHARD-02` is the\n\ncodex\n{\"status\":\"repairable_failure\",\"summary\":\"The planned dispatcher state and successor were recorded, but the repository\u2019s structural validator exposed a parsing defect in its own front-matter reader: accepted R-series list fields written as comma-delimited values are treated as one scalar, producing false provenance/requirement mismatches. I\u2019m making the narrowly scoped validator correction and will rerun the validation.\",\"changed_files\":[\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.json\",\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md\",\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/README.md\",\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/D0003.md\"],\"test_result\":\"Initial structural-validator run failed only on list-field parsing across accepted R0001\u2013R0012; bounded dispatcher and checkpoint checks passed.\",\"evidence\":{\"agent_log\":\"\",\"adapter_log\":\"\",\"test_log\":\"validate_runbook_generation.py reported comma-delimited front-matter list fields as mismatches.\",\"browser_log\":\"\",\"screenshots\":[]},\"acceptance_results\":[],\"documentation\":{\"reviewed_files\":[\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/PROJECT_BRIEF.md\",\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/specification/README.md\",\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/specification/decision-log.md\",\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md\"],\"updated_files\":[],\"summary\":\"Pending focused validator repair.\"},\"known_limitations\":[\"Structural validator parsing defect is being repaired before final validation.\"],\"browser_coverage\":\"Not applicable; this is authoring-ledger and validator work.\",\"recommended_next_step\":\"retry_qwen\"}\napply patch\npatch: completed\n/Users/simon/Dev/github/jakowicz/runbook-generator/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/validate_runbook_generation.py\ndiff --git a/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/README.md b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/README.md\nindex e4980b5b0d8712db21e8b286ae007aa785ea5cc7..8d32d54d8397dd1fcd8ec7acbe4fcd23a82d2755\n--- a/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/README.md\n+++ b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/README.md\n@@ -82,7 +82,7 @@\n ```\n \n The authoring collection starts at `authoring-runbooks/INITIAL.md`; the\n-dispatcher is `authoring-runbooks/D0001.md`. The B-series collection has its\n+dispatcher is `authoring-runbooks/D0003.md`. The B-series collection has its\n own `.state/authoring-runbooks.sqlite3` and `.state/live/` evidence locations.\n Its authoritative allocation ledger is\n [`planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.json`](planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.json),\ndiff --git a/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/D0003.md b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/D0003.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..b9566ea5c6579bdd09d3b4b122799dda6f52dfc6\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/D0003.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,70 @@\n+---\n+task_id: D0003\n+sequence: 10\n+title: Resume bounded implementation-runbook authoring dispatch after D0002\n+browser_impact: not_applicable\n+playwright_spec:\n+---\n+\n+## Objective\n+\n+Run one durable authoring-dispatch iteration after D0002. Expand at most one\n+eligible queued specification/catalogue chapter into no more than 250 `IMP-*`\n+records, validate it, then allocate ready unassigned contracts into at most ten\n+new B-series authoring tasks with no more than seven R-series outputs each.\n+Create exactly one successor dispatcher when queued work or ready contracts\n+remain; otherwise create exactly one final audit B-series task. Exit after that\n+bounded set.\n+\n+## Context packet\n+\n+Read `INITIAL.md`, `../PROJECT_BRIEF.md`, `../specification/README.md`,\n+`../planning/implementation-catalogue-index.json`,\n+`../planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.json`, its Markdown ledger, and\n+`../../../runbooks/F014.md`. Review D0002's `dispatch_history` checkpoint.\n+`SHARD-02` remains ineligible until `DEC-0004`/`GATE-0004` is explicitly\n+resolved; `SHARD-03` and `SHARD-04` retain their listed predecessor/gate blocks;\n+and `SHARD-05` remains held unless explicit authorisation is recorded.\n+\n+## Output list\n+\n+- No R-series output is preassigned. Allocate R IDs only for ready, unassigned\n+  catalogue contracts discovered after the bounded chapter check.\n+- At most ten new B-series authoring runbooks, each owning no more than seven\n+  newly assigned R-series outputs.\n+- Exactly one successor dispatcher or one final audit B-series task, selected\n+  only after the queue and ready-contract check.\n+\n+## Validation\n+\n+Validate JSON, the selected chapter's 250-contract limit, unique IMP/B/R IDs,\n+dependency closure and acyclicity, ownership/path collisions, allocation\n+uniqueness, provenance, and asset metadata. Confirm each B owns at most seven R\n+IDs and no more than ten B tasks were created. Confirm the successor/final-audit\n+choice against remaining queued chapters and ready unassigned contracts.\n+\n+## Checkpoint and update procedure\n+\n+Atomically update the JSON and Markdown ledgers with chapter state, allocations,\n+counters, and the D0003 checkpoint only after validation. Retain reserved IDs on\n+repair; never renumber, replace, or rewrite an accepted B/R contract.\n+\n+## Collision protection\n+\n+Before creating any B, R, IMP, successor, or audit path, verify that its ID and\n+path are absent from the authoritative manifest and filesystem. On collision,\n+stop without overwriting or reusing the ID.\n+\n+## Stop condition\n+\n+Stop immediately after at most one chapter expansion, one allocation wave, and\n+exactly one successor dispatcher or final audit task. Do not create R-series\n+files or materialise a whole-game plan in this dispatcher.\n+\n+## Acceptance criteria\n+\n+- The iteration expands at most one eligible chapter and adds no more than 250 IMP contracts.\n+- It creates at most ten bounded B-series authoring tasks, each with at most seven assigned R-series outputs.\n+- Every created B task has its context packet, output list, validation, checkpoint/update, collision protection, and stop condition.\n+- If queued or ready work remains, exactly one successor dispatcher is created; otherwise exactly one final audit B-series task is created.\n+- IDs, manifest ownership, provenance, asset assessments, and dependencies are validated without overwriting accepted work.\ndiff --git a/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.json b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.json\nindex 8658e5ee05d7f524f0320681a1d98c40f8af61fb..9d4b1248ff0357eb453c060771c7126c0272abcf\n--- a/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.json\n+++ b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.json\n@@ -8,7 +8,8 @@\n   \"id_counters\": {\"next_authoring_batch_id\": \"B0007\", \"next_implementation_runbook_id\": \"R0013\", \"rule\": \"Never reuse, renumber, or replace an accepted B or R ID. Append new allocations using these counters only.\"},\n   \"wave\": {\"number\": 1, \"state\": \"planned\", \"checkpoint_after_each_batch\": true, \"resume_from\": \"first batch whose state is not accepted; validate accepted IDs, paths, and provenance before dispatch\", \"recovery\": \"If a batch fails, retain its IDs, mark it blocked or repairable, repair only its listed output paths, validate its contracts, then resume that same batch. Do not reallocate its R IDs.\"},\n   \"dispatch_history\": [\n-    {\"dispatcher\":\"D0001\",\"sequence\":8,\"state\":\"complete\",\"expanded_chapter\":null,\"new_imp_contract_ids\":[],\"new_authoring_batches\":[],\"ready_unassigned_contract_ids\":[],\"queued_c